      "content": "Melanoma presentation varies significantly across skin tones. On lighter skin, it often appears as a classic, asymmetrical, multi-colored mole (ABCDE criteria). However, on darker skin, melanoma can be more subtle, sometimes presenting as a dark, brown, or black patch that may not follow the traditional rules. It's crucial to look for any new, changing, or unusual pigmented lesion regardless of skin tone to ensure thorough screening.",
